  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CF27E5">Definition <span data-tag="CF27E5">8.3.2.1</span>.</a>equivalence!of $\mathbf{S}$-enriched categories Let $\mathbf{S}$ be an monoidal model category. We say that a functor $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ in $\SCat $ is a <em>weak equivalence</em> if the induced functor $\rm {h} \it {\calC } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it {\calC '}$ is an equivalence of $\rm {h} \it {\mathbf{S}}$-enriched categories. In other words, $F$ is a weak equivalence if and only if: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For every pair of objects $X,Y \in \calC $, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calC }(X,Y) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC '}(F(X),F(Y)) \]
</div>
<p>
 is a weak equivalence in $\mathbf{S}$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Every object $Y \in \calC '$ is equivalent to $F(X)$ in the homotopy category $\rm {h} \it {\calC '}$, for some $X \in \calC $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
